{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 7, :comments ["<b>And Aaron shall burn incense upon it.</b> This commandment is not for the High Priest alone, but applies also to ordinary priests, like the rule for kindling the lamps adjacent to it (Exodus 30:8), where it likewise says, \"And when Aaron lights the lamps\" — and it is not for the High Priest alone, as it says above (Exodus 27:21), \"Aaron and his sons shall arrange it.\" And I do not know why Scripture mentions Aaron in both of them and does not say \"the priest.\" Perhaps it is because of the formulation below, \"And Aaron shall make atonement upon its horns\" (Exodus 30:10), which is for Aaron alone. Or perhaps it hints that Aaron shall be the first to perform the incense and the lamps. So too it says at the end of \"Speak to the priests\" (Leviticus 24:3), \"Aaron shall arrange it\" and does not mention his sons, because he is the first to perform it. And there Scripture mentions \"a perpetual statute\" for the commandment."], :book :exodus, :voice :ramban, :lang :en, :chapter 30, :notes {0 "Ramban cites Leviticus 24:3 with the phrase חֻקַּת עוֹלָם (\"a perpetual statute\"), which does not appear in that verse as we have it; the translation follows his text as given."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T03:18:16.044977050Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}